{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268402,"nonce":"YwzZjzomFqT4k0Qk5bSVsb+n/A0=","title":"CodeEditor needs extension points for an IDE built on it (RayDE)","message":"**What**\n\nRayDE (github.com/rayzor-blade/RayDE, a Haxe IDE; its issue bb19773) builds on ashui's CodeEditor and needs the following, in the order it needs them. Its first phase, the compilation-server display protocol and LSP, does not wait on this; showing diagnostics in the editor does. Requested through ChimpMonk's session, which says its user decided it.\n\n- Decorations: ranges with a class or style (diagnostic underlines in error, warning and info kinds; highlight ranges for references and search), replaced as a set per owner.\n- Gutter markers per line (error and warning icons, breakpoints) with a click callback.\n- Caret and selection: read and set, change events, in (line, column) and offset forms.\n- Applying text edits from code as one undo step: a list of range replacements, as from a rename or a formatter.\n- Position lookup: a text position to its on-screen rectangle and back, so popups for completion, signatures and hover can be placed; or a slot for an anchored popup, if ashui should own that.\n- Hover events at a text position after a delay.\n- Key hooks so an app can bind Ctrl-Space, F12, F2 and the like before the editor consumes them.\n- The highlighter accepting semantic tokens from a language server alongside the lexical ones.\n\n**Not covered**\n\nb8e506d is closed and was about compiler completion inside hxx templates, not editor popups, so nothing here exists yet.\n\n**To do**\n\nDesign the API once for all eight (CodeEditor is components/haxe/ashui/components/CodeEditor.hx with code/ beside it), starting with decorations and gutter markers, which diagnostics need. Each item gets a test in CodeComponents.","files":null}]}